---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
const itemSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is the Oreo Blizzard available all year?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. The Oreo Cookie Blizzard is a year-round menu item at Dairy Queen. Unlike seasonal flavors, it stays on the menu all year."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Does the Oreo Blizzard contain gluten?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. The Oreo Blizzard contains wheat from the Oreo cookie pieces. It also contains milk and soy. DQ kitchens handle multiple allergens: consult the DQ allergen guide if you have a serious allergy."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What size Oreo Blizzard should I order?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The Mini ($3.49, ~300 cal) is right for a quick taste or a light dessert after a meal. The Small ($4.49, 420 cal) is the everyday order for one person. The Medium ($5.49, 590 cal) is for a bigger appetite. The Large ($5.99, 920 cal) is best for sharing or the truly devoted."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
};
---
<Layout title="Dairy Queen Oreo Blizzard — Price, Calories & Sizes 2026" description="DQ Oreo Blizzard price 2026: Mini $3.49, Small $4.49, Medium $5.49, Large $5.99. 420 cal Small. The #1 Blizzard at DQ — full nutrition and ordering guide.">
<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(itemSchema)} />


<Breadcrumbs items={[{"name": "Home", "href": "/"}, {"name": "Menu", "href": "/categories"}, {"name": "Blizzard Treats", "href": "/categories/blizzard-treats"}, {"name": "Oreo® Blizzard"}]} />

<div class="container">
  <div class="item-hero">
    <div class="item-media">
      <img src="/Images/oreo-blizzard.webp" alt="Dairy Queen Oreo Blizzard Treat" loading="eager" width="600" height="450">
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="badge-row"><span class="badge red">Most Popular Blizzard</span><span class="badge blue">Year-Round</span><span class="badge">Served Upside Down</span></div>
      <h1>Oreo® Cookie Blizzard® Treat</h1>
      <p class="quick-answer" style="margin:10px 0 14px;padding:12px 14px;background:#F0F9FF;border-left:4px solid #0E7490;border-radius:0 10px 10px 0;font-size:.98rem;line-height:1.55;color:#0B1E38;"><strong>Quick answer:</strong> An Oreo Cookie Blizzard at Dairy Queen costs about $3.49 for a Mini, $4.49 for a Small, $5.49 for a Medium and $5.99 for a Large. A Small has about 420 calories. It is on the menu year-round. Prices vary by location.</p>
      <div class="item-price-lg">From $3.49</div>
      <p>The Oreo Cookie Blizzard is DQ vanilla soft serve blended with crushed Oreo cookies until it is thick enough to hold upside down. The cookie pieces stay crunchy, and the chocolate cookie balances the sweet soft serve, which is why it has been Dairy Queen’s best-known Blizzard for decades.</p>

      <table class="spec-table"><tbody>
        <tr><td>Ingredients</td><td>DQ vanilla soft serve, Oreo cookie pieces</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Sizes Available</td><td>Mini · Small · Medium · Large</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Starting Price</td><td>$3.49 (Mini)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Calories (Small)</td><td>420 cal</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Allergens</td><td>Milk, Wheat, Soy <span style="display:block;font-size:.8rem;color:#64748B;">Shared equipment; check <a href="/blog/dq-gluten-free-allergen-guide">our allergen guide</a> and DQ’s official list.</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Availability</td><td>Year-round at all DQ locations</td></tr>
      </tbody></table>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<section class="section section-alt">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-title">Oreo Blizzard: Price &amp; Calories by Size</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap" style="max-width:680px;margin:0 auto;">
      <table class="size-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Size</th><th>Price</th><th>Calories</th><th>Total Fat</th><th>Total Sugar</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Mini</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$3.49</td><td>~300 cal</td><td>~10g</td><td>~36g</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Small</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$4.49</td><td>420 cal</td><td>14g</td><td>52g</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Medium</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$5.49</td><td>590 cal</td><td>20g</td><td>74g</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Large</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$5.99</td><td>920 cal</td><td>31g</td><td>116g</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p style="text-align:center;margin-top:12px;font-size:.84rem;color:var(--color-text-muted);">Nutrition values are approximate. Actual values may vary by location and preparation.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container article-body">
    <h2>Why the Oreo Blizzard is DQ’s most popular flavor</h2>
    <p>The Blizzard arrived at Dairy Queen in 1985, and Oreo has been on the menu ever since. It is simple, it is not too sweet, and the cookies keep their crunch from top to bottom. If you only try one Blizzard, make it this one. See how it compares with every other flavor in our <a href="/blog/best-blizzard-flavors-ranked">Blizzard rankings</a>, or browse the full <a href="/categories/blizzard-treats">Blizzard menu</a>.</p>

    <h2>How a Blizzard is made</h2>
    <p>Staff put soft serve and Oreo pieces in a cup and blend them on a mixer with a long spindle, so the cookies end up all the way through instead of sitting on top. Two things to know:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Even mix-ins:</strong> blending breaks the cookies into a mix of crumbs and bigger pieces, so you get cookie in every bite.</li>
      <li><strong>Thick enough to flip:</strong> a well-made Blizzard is thick enough to hold upside down, and many stores hand it over that way.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Oreo Blizzard vs. Royal Oreo Blizzard</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table">
      <thead><tr><th></th><th>Standard Oreo® Blizzard</th><th>Royal Oreo® Blizzard</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>Price</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$3.49 (Mini) / $4.49 (Small)</td><td class="price-cell">$3.99 (Mini) / $4.99 (Small)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Center</strong></td><td>Oreo pieces blended through</td><td>Hot fudge-filled center</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Texture</strong></td><td>Crunchy cookie in every bite</td><td>Crunchy cookie plus gooey fudge</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Calories (Small)</strong></td><td>420 cal</td><td>490 cal</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table></div>

    <h2>Ways to customize your Oreo Blizzard</h2>
    <p>Oreo is an easy flavor to build on. A few popular tweaks (most add a small charge):</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Extra Oreo:</strong> ask for more cookie pieces if you like more crunch.</li>
      <li><strong>Add cookie dough:</strong> half Oreo, half cookie dough is one of the best-known <a href="/blog/dairy-queen-secret-menu">secret menu</a> combos.</li>
      <li><strong>Chocolate soft serve:</strong> some stores can make it with chocolate soft serve for a darker, more chocolatey Blizzard.</li>
      <li><strong>Hot fudge center:</strong> order the <a href="/items/royal-oreo-blizzard">Royal Oreo</a> instead for a fudge-filled middle.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Oreo Blizzard vs. other chocolate Blizzards</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="size-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Blizzard</th><th>Mini Price</th><th>Small Cal</th><th>What it tastes like</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Oreo® Cookie Blizzard</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$3.49</td><td>420</td><td>Crunchy chocolate cookie, not too sweet</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Royal Oreo® Blizzard</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$3.99</td><td>490</td><td>Oreo plus a hot fudge center</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong><a href="/items/choco-brownie-blizzard">Choco Brownie Extreme</a></strong></td><td class="price-cell">$3.99</td><td>510</td><td>Brownie pieces, fudge and chocolate chunks</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong><a href="/items/brownie-batter-blizzard">Brownie Batter Blizzard</a></strong></td><td class="price-cell">$3.99</td><td>530</td><td>Brownie batter and chocolate</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong><a href="/items/mint-oreo-blizzard">Mint Oreo® Blizzard</a></strong></td><td class="price-cell">$3.49</td><td>~440</td><td>Mint and Oreo cookie</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Is the Oreo Blizzard available all year?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
      <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">Yes. The Oreo Cookie Blizzard is a year-round menu item at Dairy Queen. Unlike seasonal flavors, it stays on the menu all year.</div></div></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Does the Oreo Blizzard contain gluten?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
      <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">Yes. The Oreo Blizzard contains wheat from the Oreo cookie pieces. It also contains milk and soy. DQ kitchens handle multiple allergens: consult the DQ allergen guide if you have a serious allergy.</div></div></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">What size Oreo Blizzard should I order?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
      <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">The Mini ($3.49, ~300 cal) is right for a quick taste or a light dessert after a meal. The Small ($4.49, 420 cal) is the everyday order for one person. The Medium ($5.49, 590 cal) is for a bigger appetite. The Large ($5.99, 920 cal) is best for sharing or the truly devoted.</div></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</Layout>
